---
import { sourceRoleStyle } from '@/lib/specimen-roles';
export interface Props { pane?: string }
const { pane = 'b' } = Astro.props;
const checklistId = `${pane}-reading-checklist`;
---
<section class="showcase-section" aria-label={`${pane.toUpperCase()} · Reading specimen`} data-specimen="reading">
  <header><h3>Webpage</h3><p>Body copy, secondary text, links, selection, and simple callouts.</p></header>
  <article class="reading" data-preview-surface data-role="body" style={sourceRoleStyle('body')}>
    <nav class="reading-nav" aria-label={`${pane.toUpperCase()} · Sample publication`}><strong>Fieldnotes</strong><a href={`#${checklistId}`} data-role="link" style={sourceRoleStyle('link')}>Reading list ↗</a></nav>
    <h4>Make room for focused work</h4>
    <p class="meta" data-role="muted" style={sourceRoleStyle('muted')}>Field notes · A short sample article</p>
    <p>A familiar workspace should help you find the next useful detail. A heading introduces the subject, a comment explains a decision, and a link offers a way to explore further. Each has a different job.</p>
    <p>When comparing palettes, <strong>keep the reading conditions steady</strong>: the same words, line length, type size, and spacing. Notice how easily you can return to the text after looking away. Then inspect any role that feels faint or distracting.</p>
    <blockquote data-role="comment" style={sourceRoleStyle('comment')}>Give the content a clear rhythm, and leave enough quiet space for a difficult idea.</blockquote>
    <p>Use the <a href={`#${checklistId}`} data-role="link" style={sourceRoleStyle('link')}>review checklist</a> below. An inline setting such as <code data-role="code-surface" style={sourceRoleStyle('code-surface')}>view=reading</code> is part of the text, while a longer example gets its own space.</p>
    <h5>A small, repeatable review</h5>
    <pre data-role="code-surface" style={sourceRoleStyle('code-surface')}><code>review:
  specimen: reading
  reference: dracula
  candidate: nord</code></pre>
    <aside class="callout" data-role="link" style={sourceRoleStyle('link')} aria-label={`${pane.toUpperCase()} · Sample information callout`}><strong>ⓘ Information:</strong> This sample configuration stays the same in both panes; it does not report the current selection.</aside>
    <aside class="callout" data-role="warning" style={sourceRoleStyle('warning')} aria-label={`${pane.toUpperCase()} · Sample warning callout`}><strong>! Caution:</strong> Comfortable body text does not guarantee legible comments, selected text, links, or controls. Inspect those pairs separately.</aside>
    <h5 id={checklistId}>Review checklist</h5>
    <ul><li>Read a complete paragraph before changing the palette.</li><li>Check the <mark data-role="selection" style={sourceRoleStyle('selection')}>selected phrase in its surrounding sentence</mark>.</li><li>Follow the underlined link with the keyboard and check its focus outline.</li></ul>
    <p class="visited-sample"><span data-role="visited-link" style={sourceRoleStyle('visited-link')}>Visited-link role sample</span></p>
    <p class="meta" data-role="muted" style={sourceRoleStyle('muted')}>The visited-link sample demonstrates a palette role; it does not read your browsing history. Selected text uses the regular foreground on the selection surface.</p>
  </article>
</section>
<style>
  .showcase-section { border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: .75rem; background: var(--surface); padding: 1rem; display: grid; gap: .75rem; min-width: 0; }
  header { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: .7rem; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  h3, header p { margin: 0; font-size: .875rem; line-height: 1.5; }
  .reading { box-sizing: border-box; padding: 1.4em; border-radius: .5rem; color-scheme: var(--tt-color-scheme,normal); font: var(--specimen-size,14px)/1.7 var(--font-sans); max-width: 66ch; width: 100%; min-width: 0; justify-self: center; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  .reading-nav { display:flex; justify-content:space-between; flex-wrap:wrap; gap:.6rem; padding-bottom:1em; margin-bottom:1.5em; border-bottom:1px solid currentColor; }
  .reading h4 { margin: 0 0 .5em; font-size: 1.6em; line-height: 1.25; letter-spacing: -.015em; }
  .reading h5 { margin: 1.3em 0 .4em; font-size: 1.15em; line-height: 1.4; }
  .reading p { margin: 0 0 1em; }
  .reading .meta { line-height: 1.6; }
  .reading strong { font-weight: 700; }
  .reading a { text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: .2em; text-decoration-thickness: 1px; }
  .reading a:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid currentColor; outline-offset: 3px; border-radius: .1em; }
  .reading blockquote { margin: 1.2em 0; padding: .3em .8em; border-inline-start: 3px solid currentColor; font-style: italic; }
  .reading code { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 1em; }
  .reading p code { padding: .05em .25em; border: 1px solid currentColor; border-radius: .2em; }
  .reading pre { margin: 0 0 1em; padding: .7em .9em; border: 1px solid currentColor; border-radius: .35em; white-space: pre-wrap; overflow-wrap: anywhere; line-height: 1.6; }
  .reading .callout { margin: 1em 0; padding: .6em .8em; border-inline-start: 3px solid currentColor; border-radius: .2em; }
  .reading ul { margin: 0 0 1em; padding-inline-start: 1.4em; }
  .reading li { margin: .35em 0; }
  .reading mark { padding: .05em .15em; border-radius: .1em; }
  .visited-sample span { text-decoration: underline dotted; text-underline-offset: .2em; }
  .reading ::selection { color: var(--role-selection-fg,var(--tt-foreground)); background: var(--role-selection-bg,var(--tt-selection)); }
  @media(max-width: 30rem) { .reading { padding: 1em; } }
</style>
